findings.body:
**Claimed critical; verifier found:** verifier off

`InsecureSkipVerify: true` is hardcoded in `NewClient()` with no staging/prod gate. Every caller gets a client that accepts any certificate, so an on-path attacker can intercept or modify ledger traffic (credentials, transfers, balances).

A comment and TICKET-77 do not constrain deployment: the same constructor will ship insecure verify into production if this package is linked there.

**Fix:** trust the staging CA (or pin the cert) via `tls.Config.RootCAs`, or gate the skip explicitly and default to verify:

```go
func NewClient(insecure bool) *http.Client {
    tlsCfg := &tls.Config{MinVersion: tls.VersionTLS12}
    if insecure {
        tlsCfg.InsecureSkipVerify = true // staging only
    }
    return &http.Client{
        Timeout: 10 * time.Second,
        Transport: &http.Transport{
            Proxy:           http.ProxyFromEnvironment,
            TLSClientConfig: tlsCfg,
        },
    }
}
```

Do not merge a global skip-verify on a shared client factory.
